# Manual exercise of POST /api/schedules/optimize (GRID-124).
# Open in VS Code with the REST Client extension, or JetBrains' HTTP client,
# and click "Send Request" above each block in order.
#
# IMPORTANT - the timestamps below expire.
# The optimizer prices a job against its baseline hour, so a job whose
# originalStartTime falls outside the current 48-hour horizon is rejected with
# 400 ("falls outside the optimization horizon"). The dates here were written
# for 2026-10-18 UTC. Before sending, replace them with the current UTC day and
# the next. Get today's UTC date with:
#     date -u +%Y-%m-%d
# Keep every originalStartTime between now and now + horizonHours.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Log in. Uses the auto-created, pre-verified admin account from
### DataInitializer, which skips the email OTP step.
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "admin@datacenter.io",
    "password": "Admin@2026!"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. The main case: inline jobs, mixed outcomes.
### Expect 200. The wide-flex job moves to the cheapest hour in its window
### (RESCHEDULED), the pinned job stays put (UNCHANGED_EXEMPT), and the
### zero-window job cannot move (UNCHANGED_ALREADY_OPTIMAL).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedules/optimize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobs": [
    {
      "id": 101,
      "name": "LLM fine-tuning, flexible",
      "cpuHours": 2000.0,
      "gpuHours": 200.0,
      "originalStartTime": "2026-10-18T14:00:00",
      "deadline": "2026-10-19T18:00:00",
      "flexibilityWindowHours": 12,
      "isExempt": false
    },
    {
      "id": 102,
      "name": "Regulatory batch, must not move",
      "cpuHours": 100.0,
      "gpuHours": 10.0,
      "originalStartTime": "2026-10-18T17:00:00",
      "deadline": "2026-10-19T18:00:00",
      "flexibilityWindowHours": 12,
      "isExempt": true
    },
    {
      "id": 103,
      "name": "Inflexible nightly job",
      "cpuHours": 50.0,
      "gpuHours": 5.0,
      "originalStartTime": "2026-10-18T20:00:00",
      "deadline": "2026-10-19T06:00:00",
      "flexibilityWindowHours": 0,
      "isExempt": false
    }
  ],
  "clusterCapacity": {
    "maxConcurrentCpuHours": 5000.0,
    "maxConcurrentGpuHours": 1000.0
  },
  "forecastLocation": "LZ_NORTH",
  "horizonHours": 48
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. A job that cannot be placed (GRID-124 AC5).
### Deadline is only 30 minutes out, but a job occupies a full hour, so no slot
### fits. Expect 200 (NOT an error) with perJobStatus
### UNCHANGED_NO_FEASIBLE_SLOT and the job still at its original time.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedules/optimize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobs": [
    {
      "id": 201,
      "name": "Impossible deadline",
      "cpuHours": 100.0,
      "gpuHours": 0.0,
      "originalStartTime": "2026-10-18T14:00:00",
      "deadline": "2026-10-18T14:30:00",
      "flexibilityWindowHours": 6,
      "isExempt": false
    }
  ],
  "horizonHours": 48
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Capacity binding. Three jobs of 200 CPU-hours each want the same cheap
### hour, but the ceiling is 250, so only one fits there and the others take
### the next-cheapest hours they can reach. Expect 200.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedules/optimize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobs": [
    {"id": 301, "name": "Contender A", "cpuHours": 200.0, "gpuHours": 0.0,
     "originalStartTime": "2026-10-18T14:00:00", "deadline": "2026-10-19T18:00:00",
     "flexibilityWindowHours": 14, "isExempt": false},
    {"id": 302, "name": "Contender B", "cpuHours": 200.0, "gpuHours": 0.0,
     "originalStartTime": "2026-10-18T14:00:00", "deadline": "2026-10-19T18:00:00",
     "flexibilityWindowHours": 14, "isExempt": false},
    {"id": 303, "name": "Contender C", "cpuHours": 200.0, "gpuHours": 0.0,
     "originalStartTime": "2026-10-18T14:00:00", "deadline": "2026-10-19T18:00:00",
     "flexibilityWindowHours": 14, "isExempt": false}
  ],
  "clusterCapacity": {"maxConcurrentCpuHours": 250.0, "maxConcurrentGpuHours": 64.0},
  "horizonHours": 48
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. The stored-jobs flow, which is what the end-to-end test uses.
### First create a job through the job API...
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/jobs
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Stored flexible job",
  "cpuHours": 1500.0,
  "gpuHours": 150.0,
  "originalStartTime": "2026-10-18T17:00:00",
  "deadline": "2026-10-19T20:00:00",
  "flexibilityWindowHours": 10,
  "isExempt": false
}

### ...then optimize with no jobs field at all. The optimizer picks up every
### eligible job this operator owns. Expect 200.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedules/optimize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### See what the optimizer is working from
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/jobs
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. Error cases. Each should return 400 with a message naming the offending
### field, and "data": null - never a partial schedule.

### Expect 400: deadline before originalStartTime
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedules/optimize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobs": [
    {"id": 1, "name": "bad", "cpuHours": 10.0, "gpuHours": 0.0,
     "originalStartTime": "2026-10-18T14:00:00", "deadline": "2026-10-18T09:00:00",
     "flexibilityWindowHours": 0, "isExempt": false}
  ]
}

### Expect 400: neither cpuHours nor gpuHours above zero
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedules/optimize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobs": [
    {"id": 1, "name": "bad", "cpuHours": 0.0, "gpuHours": 0.0,
     "originalStartTime": "2026-10-18T14:00:00", "deadline": "2026-10-19T09:00:00",
     "flexibilityWindowHours": 0, "isExempt": false}
  ]
}

### Expect 400: horizonHours outside 1-168
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedules/optimize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"horizonHours": 200}

### Expect 400: explicitly empty job set
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedules/optimize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"jobs": []}

### Expect 403: no token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedules/optimize
Content-Type: application/json

{"jobs": []}
